(set-info :smt-lib-version 2.6)
(set-logic QF_FPLRA)
(set-info :source |
Translated by: Andrew Teylu <andrew@tey.lu>
Translated on: 2026-08-24
Application: Floating-point translations of existing SMT-LIB QF_LRA Latendresse benchmarks, which originate in flux-balance-analysis and pathway-database model-completion applications [1,2].
Target solver: cvc5
Time limit: 300

This benchmark is a new QF_FPLRA floating-point translation of the existing SMT-LIB benchmark non-incremental/QF_LRA/latendresse/shewanella-compact2b.smt2. The underlying QF_LRA benchmark was not generated for this submission and is not resubmitted here; only this floating-point translation is new.

The source is an authentic compact Shewanella instance with 52 bounded discrete selectors, no reaction gates, one top-level constraint conjunction, and a signed selector-only objective.
The existing QF_LRA source declares status sat; that status is provenance information only and is not copied as a claim about this translation.

This file is a structural mixed floating-point/linear-real translation using QF_FPLRA. Real variables are replaced by (_ FloatingPoint 4 4) variables and arithmetic over them uses roundNearestTiesToEven. Numeric constants remain exact Reals beneath SMT-LIB to_fp conversions. Linear comparisons become floating-point comparisons; equality uses IEEE fp.eq. No finite-value guards are added.

Floating point is not the reals; satisfiability is not assumed to survive this translation. The translated status is unknown.

[1] Timothy King, Clark Barrett, and Bruno Dutertre, Simplex with Sum of Infeasibilities for SMT, FMCAD 2013.
[2] Mario Latendresse, Markus Krummenacker, Miles Trupp, and Peter D. Karp, Construction and completion of flux balance models from pathway databases, Bioinformatics 28(3), 388-396, 2012.
|)
